## Execution at a Real Boundary

Every regression scenario drives one of the Real Boundaries this repository declares under `## Real Boundaries` in `.adw/scenarios.md`: its real runtime, a real browser, the built artifact or a real command-line invocation. Its phrases set up, drive or observe that boundary from outside the application's own process. Behaviour provable inside the test process, by calling a function, a module or a phase with stand-ins around it, belongs to unit tests alone, and no phrase is registered for it.

## Given — Setup

| # | Phrase | Semantics |
|---|--------|-----------|
| G1 | `a subprocess fixture is loaded for {string}` | Configures the CLI stub to replay a named fixture file before spawning the subprocess under test |
| G2 | `the mock server is configured to accept {string} requests` | Seeds mock-server state so the named HTTP method + path returns a 2xx response |

## When — Invocation

| # | Phrase | Semantics |
|---|--------|-----------|
| W1 | `the {string} subprocess is invoked with args {string}` | Spawns the named CLI entry-point with the given argument string and captures its exit code |

## Then — Observed Outcomes

| # | Phrase | Semantics |
|---|--------|-----------|
| T1 | `the subprocess exits {int}` | Asserts the captured exit code equals the expected value |
| T2 | `the mock server recorded a {string} request to {string}` | Asserts that the process under test sent the mock server at least one request with the given method and path |
